Talk to chips on an I2C bus through /dev/i2cN

Syntax:
    smbctl [-d /dev/i2cN] [-j] COMMAND ...

Options:
    -d dev      I2C device (default /dev/i2c0)
    -j          print results as JSON, one object per line

Commands:
    scan                       list chips that answer (0x08..0x77), probing
                               with Receive Byte
    get   ADDR REG             read one byte register
    set   ADDR REG VALUE       write one byte register
    getw  ADDR REG             read a 16-bit register, low byte first
                               (SMBus Read Word)
    setw  ADDR REG VALUE       write a 16-bit register, low byte first
    read  ADDR REG [COUNT]     read COUNT bytes from REG on
    write ADDR REG BYTE...     write bytes from REG on
    recv  ADDR [COUNT]         read with no register byte
    dump  ADDR [LEN]           hex dump of registers 0..LEN-1 (default 256);
                               uses block reads, or byte reads if the
                               controller can't do them
    temp  ADDR                 LM75/TMP105-style temperature (register 0)
    watch ADDR REG MS [COUNT]  read REG every MS ms and print it when it
                               changes; reopens the device if the driver
                               restarts
    info                       what the driver reports about itself

Numbers take C syntax (0x48 or 72).
Exit status: 0 success, 1 the transfer or the device failed, 2 bad usage.

Examples:
    smbctl scan
    smbctl temp 0x48
    smbctl dump 0x50 128
    smbctl -j get 0x48 1
